      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Magic-angle twisted bilayer graphene revealed a tunable route to flat bands and correlated phases, opening a major new field in two-dimensional quantum materials.",
        "attribution": "Bistritzer and MacDonald supplied the key theoretical prediction; Jarillo-Herrero's group established the experimental platform and its correlated states. The proposed trio captures the theory–experiment chain.",
        "maturity": "The central phenomena have been intensively studied and reproduced across devices, though the field's phase diagram and mechanisms continue to develop.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The microscopic origins of some observed phases remain disputed, and the boundary between foundational discovery and subsequent developments is not sharp."
        ]
      }
    },
