      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Optical lattice clocks combine remarkable precision with a new way to probe fundamental physics and potentially redefine timekeeping.",
        "attribution": "Katori pioneered the lattice-clock concept and its clock transition; Ye made major complementary advances in precision and performance. The two have clear, distinct claims.",
        "maturity": "Clocks have reached extraordinary stability and accuracy, with independent implementations and applications, though international adoption as a time standard remains a longer process.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The discovery-to-technology case is strong, but the relative weight of the original concept and subsequent precision engineering requires judgment."
        ]
      }
    },
